{
 "A party relying on electronic evidence shall preserve the original electronic record until the conclusion of the proceeding.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>Chapter VI</1>The Arbitral Tribunal": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>Chapter VII</1>Arbitral Proceedings & Awards": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "In an arbitration other than an international commercial arbitration, the award shall be made within twelve months from the date of completion of pleadings, which the parties may by consent extend by up to six months, in accordance with Section {0}A of the Act. In an international commercial arbitration, the tribunal shall endeavour to make the award within the same period.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>Chapter VIII</1>Mediation Procedure": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Where the other party does not accept the request within fifteen days, the requesting party may treat the request as rejected. Mediation sessions may be held in person or online.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>Chapter IX</1>Conciliation Procedure": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>Chapter X</1>Specialized Corporate ADR": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>Chapter XI</1>Implementation and Enforcement": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "An award shall be enforced in accordance with Section {0} of the Act, in the same manner as if it were a decree of a court. The filing of an application to set aside the award shall not by itself render it unenforceable, unless the court grants a stay.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>Chapter XII</1>Costs & Fees": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>Chapter XIII</1>Miscellaneous": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "The Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure, {0} is hereby superseded.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "A proceeding commenced before this Code came into force shall continue under the Code in force at its commencement, unless the parties agree that this Code shall apply.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Where an agreement refers disputes to the Code of the Institute without specifying an edition, the edition in force on the date of commencement of the proceeding shall apply.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "The Adjudix Rule Book · Third Edition": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Builds on {0} to cover every mechanism the Institute offers, online, offline, and hybrid.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>VII.</1> Emergency Arbitration": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>VIII.</1> Arbitral Proceedings & Awards": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>IX.</1> Mediation Procedure": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>X.</1> Conciliation Procedure": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>X-A.</1> Adjudix Lok Adalat": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Sections {0}A–{1}C": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Hybrid Processes (Med-Arb)": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>XI.</1> Mediation-Arbitration (Med-Arb) Protocol": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>XII.</1> Specialized Corporate ADR": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Part VII": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>XIII.</1> Implementation and Enforcement": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>XIV.</1> Costs & Fees": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>XV.</1> Miscellaneous": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "WHEREAS the resolution of disputes by consent, by conciliation, and by the binding decision of a neutral chosen by the parties is an essential complement to the courts, and the confidence of the public in such resolution rests on the integrity of the institutions that administer it;": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "WHEREAS Adjudix Dispute Resolution Institute has, since the first edition of this Code in {0} and its second edition in {1}, administered arbitration, mediation, conciliation, and corporate dispute resolution in person and online, and has now extended its services to emergency arbitration, the hybrid model of Mediation-Arbitration, the Adjudix Lok Adalat, and the implementation of awards and settlements in India and throughout the world;": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "WHEREAS innovation in the means of resolving disputes must never be purchased at the cost of fairness, and every new procedure adopted by the Institute must offer the parties at least the same protection as the procedures it supplements;": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "AND WHEREAS the Institute considers it necessary to declare, in authoritative and binding terms, the Moral Principles upon which every proceeding under its administration is conducted;": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "NOW, THEREFORE, the Institute declares the following Moral Principles, which form the foundation of this Code. They bind the Institute, its governing body, its Secretariat and staff, and every arbitrator, emergency arbitrator, mediator, conciliator, expert, and other person acting under this Code. Every provision of this Code shall be interpreted, and every discretion under it exercised, in the manner that best gives effect to these Principles. Where any provision is ambiguous, the interpretation most consistent with these Principles shall prevail.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Equality of Parties and Procedural Fairness": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Confidentiality and Discretion": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Integrity and Probity": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Efficiency and Proportionality": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Transparency of Rules and Fees": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "IX": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Innovation with Integrity": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "X": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Technology and Data Stewardship": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "XI": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Finality and Implementation": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "XII": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Accessibility": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "XIII": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "DECLARATION. Every neutral shall, on accepting an appointment under this Code, subscribe to the following declaration: “I have read the Moral Principles of the Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure, {0}. I am independent of the parties and impartial between them, and I have disclosed every circumstance that the Principles require me to disclose. I will conduct this proceeding fairly, diligently, and in confidence, and I will abide by these Principles throughout it.”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "“Adjudix Lok Adalat”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "means the confidential settlement sitting described in Chapter X-A.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "includes an interim award, a partial award, and an award on agreed terms, but does not include an order of an emergency arbitrator.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "“emergency arbitrator”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "means an arbitrator appointed under Chapter VII.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "“Med-Arb”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "means the hybrid procedure of mediation followed, where settlement is not reached, by arbitration, under Part V.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "means an arbitrator, emergency arbitrator, mediator, or conciliator appointed under this Code.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "It governs arbitration, emergency arbitration, mediation, conciliation, the Adjudix Lok Adalat, Med-Arb, and corporate dispute resolution administered by the Institute, whether conducted in person, online, or partly in each, and the implementation of their outcomes.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The Secretariat shall disclose to the parties any automated or artificial-intelligence tool used in administering their proceeding and the purpose for which it is used. No such tool shall decide any question affecting the rights of a party, which shall be decided only by the neutral.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The E-Portal may offer the parties assisted online negotiation before or alongside a proceeding. A settlement reached through it may be recorded under this Code, and nothing said or offered in the course of it shall be relied on in any later proceeding.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Any document required to be signed under this Code, including an award, may be signed by an electronic signature or electronic authentication technique recognised under the Information Technology Act, {0}.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The Secretariat may verify the identity of any participant, including by one-time password or digital identity verification, before granting access to the E-Portal or to a virtual hearing.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "An award signed electronically shall be authenticated by the Secretariat and a certified copy furnished to each party.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The Secretariat shall maintain the E-Portal with reasonable security practices and procedures, and shall restrict access to the record of each proceeding to the parties, their representatives, the neutral, and authorised staff.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Personal data shall be processed in accordance with the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, {0}, and only for the purposes of the proceeding and its implementation.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The Secretariat shall publish its policies on access to, retention of, and destruction of records. A party may obtain a copy of the record of its proceeding in an accessible electronic format.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "No participant shall record a virtual hearing, or capture or disseminate any part of it, except as directed under <1>Section {0}</1>.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Where the same tribunal is constituted in two or more proceedings that raise a common question of law or fact, the tribunal may, on a party's application and after consulting all parties, conduct them concurrently or one after another, hear them together, or suspend any of them pending the determination of another. Each proceeding remains separate, and a separate award shall be made in each, unless the parties agree otherwise.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "At the conference, the neutral shall, after hearing the parties, settle the procedural timetable, the manner of taking evidence, whether hearings will be in person, virtual, or hybrid, the suitability of the fast-track procedure, and any other procedural matter. The timetable, and any modification of it, shall be communicated to the Secretariat and the parties.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The neutral may ask the parties to submit case management proposals before the conference, and may request that each party attend in person or through an internal representative with authority to take procedural decisions.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The neutral shall also enquire whether the parties wish to explore settlement, including through mediation, an Adjudix Lok Adalat sitting, or, where they have so agreed, the Med-Arb Protocol.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The neutral shall consult the parties on the measures needed to protect the security of information exchanged in the proceeding and may give directions on them. A party that fails to comply with such directions may be ordered to bear the resulting costs.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Conduct of Virtual, Physical, and Hybrid Hearings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Hearings may be conducted in person, as virtual hearings, or as hybrid hearings, as the neutral directs after consulting the parties, having regard to the nature of the evidence, the location of the participants, and cost.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "A virtual or hybrid hearing shall be conducted so that every participant can see and hear every other participant and the documents under consideration. The neutral may issue a protocol on the presence of persons in each participant's room, the sharing of documents, and the examination of witnesses, and shall ensure that no party is prejudiced by the medium.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "In an arbitration, an oral hearing shall be held if a party so requests, in accordance with Section {0} of the Act; otherwise the tribunal may, after consulting the parties, decide the dispute on documents and written submissions alone.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The neutral is not bound by the Code of Civil Procedure, {0} or the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, {1}, but shall be guided by the principles of natural justice.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The neutral may, after consulting the parties, appoint one or more experts to report on specific issues, and the parties may present expert witnesses of their own. Experts may be directed to confer and prepare a joint statement of matters agreed and not agreed.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Digital and Electronic Evidence Standards": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Electronic records, including emails, messages, metadata, and data from electronic systems, may be relied upon as evidence. The neutral may require such certification as to the source and integrity of an electronic record as the neutral considers appropriate, guided by Section {0} of the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, {1}.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "A party relying on electronic evidence shall preserve the original electronic record, in its native format, until the conclusion of the proceeding and any challenge to its outcome.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Where a party is a frequent user of the Institute, the Secretariat shall disclose to the other parties, on request, the number of proceedings involving that party in which the proposed arbitrator has been appointed in the preceding three years, and shall rotate appointments in such proceedings so that no neutral becomes dependent on the repeat appointments of one party.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Where the Secretariat is to appoint a sole arbitrator, it shall propose to the parties three eligible neutrals from the Panel suited to the subject matter of the dispute, and each party may rank them in order of first, second, and third preference within seven days. The neutral with the best combined ranking shall be appointed; where the rankings are tied or are not returned in time, the appointment shall be made by draw of lots from the three neutrals proposed.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Where the Secretariat is to constitute a tribunal of three arbitrators, the tribunal shall include at least one Chartered Accountant, Company Secretary, or engineer where the subject matter of the dispute so requires, and the Secretariat shall make each appointment by draw of lots from the eligible neutrals on the Panel of the relevant profession.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Every draw of lots shall be random, shall be conducted by the Secretariat in the presence of, or by video link open to, the parties or their representatives, and shall be recorded in writing together with the names of every neutral included in the draw; the record shall be furnished to any party, and to any court, on request.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Each party shall promptly disclose to the Secretariat, the tribunal, and the other parties the existence and identity of any person not a party who has agreed to fund its claim or defence and has an economic interest in the outcome, so that arbitrators can fulfil their duty of disclosure. After the tribunal has been constituted, no party shall enter into a funding arrangement that would give rise to a conflict of interest with a member of the tribunal, and the tribunal may take any funding arrangement into account in apportioning costs.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Each party shall promptly inform the Secretariat, the tribunal, and the other parties of any change in its representation. The tribunal may, after giving the parties an opportunity to comment, take any measure necessary to avoid a conflict of interest of an arbitrator arising from such a change, including excluding a new representative from the proceeding in whole or in part.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>Chapter VII</1>Emergency Arbitration": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Application for Emergency Relief": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "A party in need of urgent interim relief that cannot await the constitution of the arbitral tribunal may file an application for emergency relief with the Secretariat, whether before or after filing the request under this Code.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The application shall set out the names and contact details of the parties and their representatives; the agreement under which the dispute is referred; a description of the dispute and of the claims known at the time; the emergency measures sought; the reasons why they cannot await the constitution of the tribunal; why harm not adequately reparable by an award of damages is likely if they are refused, and how that harm outweighs the harm to the other party; and why the applicant has a reasonable possibility of success on the merits. It shall be accompanied by the emergency arbitrator's fee and the emergency administrative fee in full.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The applicant shall serve a copy of the application on every other party at the time of filing, unless it applies for, and justifies, relief without prior notice.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Where the application is made before the request for commencement, the applicant shall file the request within ten days of filing the application, failing which the Secretariat shall terminate the emergency proceeding.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "This Chapter applies to every agreement that refers disputes to this Code, unless the parties have agreed to exclude it; and to an agreement made before this Code came into force only if the parties so agree. Nothing in it prevents a party from seeking interim measures from a court under Section {0} of the Act.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Appointment of Emergency Arbitrator": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The Secretariat shall appoint an emergency arbitrator from the Panel within two days of receiving a complete application.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Before accepting the appointment, the emergency arbitrator shall sign a statement of acceptance, availability, impartiality, and independence and make the written disclosure required by this Code. A challenge to the emergency arbitrator shall be made within one business day of the party being informed of the appointment, or of the circumstances giving rise to the challenge, and shall be decided by the Secretariat after giving the emergency arbitrator and the other parties an opportunity to comment.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "If the emergency arbitrator is replaced, the substitute shall decide whether to resume the proceeding at the stage reached or to begin it again.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Unless the parties agree otherwise, the emergency arbitrator shall not act as an arbitrator in any subsequent arbitration relating to the dispute.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Emergency Proceedings and Timelines": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The emergency arbitrator shall, within two days of appointment, fix a schedule for the consideration of the application, which shall ordinarily be heard by video conference.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The emergency arbitrator shall have the powers of an arbitral tribunal under <1>Section {0}</1>, and may make an order subject to conditions, including the provision of appropriate security. The emergency arbitrator shall decide any objection to jurisdiction for the purposes of the application, without prejudice to the tribunal's later decision.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The order shall be in writing, dated, signed, and reasoned, and shall fix the costs of the emergency proceeding and which party shall bear them, subject to the final decision of the tribunal. It shall be made within fifteen days of appointment, which the Secretariat may extend on a reasoned request in exceptional circumstances.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Where giving notice would defeat the purpose of the relief, the applicant may seek a protective preliminary order, without notice to the other party, directing that party not to frustrate the relief sought. The emergency arbitrator shall decide the request within twenty-four hours of appointment. The applicant shall serve the application, the order, and all related communications on every other party within twelve hours of receiving the order, failing which the order lapses three days after it is made; and the other party shall be heard at the earliest opportunity, after which the emergency arbitrator may confirm, modify, or revoke it.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Enforceability and Modification of Emergency Orders": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "An order of an emergency arbitrator binds the parties from the date it is made. The parties undertake to comply with it without delay.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "In an arbitration seated in India, an order of an emergency arbitrator is an order under Section {0}({1}) of the Act and is enforceable under Section {2}({3}) of the Act, as held by the Supreme Court of India.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "A party that obtains emergency relief shall immediately disclose any material change in the circumstances on which it was sought or granted. Before the tribunal is constituted, the emergency arbitrator may, on a reasoned request and after hearing the parties, modify or revoke the order.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The order does not bind the arbitral tribunal on any question decided in it. The tribunal, once constituted, may confirm, modify, or set aside the order, and shall decide any claim concerning compliance with it and the reallocation of its costs. The order ceases to bind the parties if a challenge to the emergency arbitrator is upheld, on the final award unless the tribunal decides otherwise, if the claim is withdrawn, or if the tribunal is not constituted within ninety days of the order.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>Chapter VIII</1>Arbitral Proceedings & Awards": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "In a fast-track arbitration, the tribunal shall hold the case management conference within fifteen days of its constitution; no party may make a new claim without the tribunal's leave; and the tribunal may, after consulting the parties, decline requests for document production and limit the number, length, and scope of written submissions and witness statements.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Where the amount in dispute does not exceed the small-claims limit fixed in the Schedule of Fees, the fast-track procedure shall apply unless a party objects in its first submission or the Secretariat, on a party's application, directs otherwise having regard to the complexity of the dispute. In such a case the award shall ordinarily be made within three months of the constitution of the tribunal, and fees shall be charged at the reduced rates fixed for small claims.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The tribunal may, on a party's application and after hearing the parties, decide any issue of fact or law as a preliminary question, by a partial award under Section {0}({1}) of the Act or by an order, where the parties agree, where doing so is likely to save time or costs, or where the circumstances otherwise warrant it. A preliminary question so accepted shall be decided within ninety days of the application.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "If, during the arbitration, the parties settle the dispute, including through mediation, an Adjudix Lok Adalat sitting, or the Med-Arb Protocol, the tribunal shall terminate the proceedings and, if requested by the parties, record the settlement as an arbitral award on agreed terms under Section {0} of the Act.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Before signing, the tribunal shall submit the draft award to the Secretariat for scrutiny. The Secretariat may require modifications as to the form of the award and, without affecting the tribunal's liberty of decision, may draw its attention to points of substance. The Secretariat shall complete its scrutiny within ten days so that no statutory time limit is put at risk. A signed copy of the award shall be delivered to each party.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>Chapter IX</1>Mediation Procedure": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Where the parties have agreed to mediate under this Code, mediation commences on the date the Secretariat receives a party's request for mediation. In any other case, it commences when the other party accepts the request. Mediation shall be conducted in accordance with this Code and the Mediation Act, {0}, to the extent applicable.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Unless the parties agree to extend it, the mediation shall be completed within one hundred and twenty days of the first appearance before the mediator.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Where the parties reach a settlement, it shall be reduced to writing as a mediated settlement agreement, signed by the parties and authenticated by the mediator.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "A mediated settlement agreement is final and binding on the parties and enforceable in accordance with the Mediation Act, {0}, to the extent applicable, or, where the parties so agree, may be executed as a settlement agreement under Section {1} of the Act with the status and effect provided by Section {2} of the Act.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>Chapter X</1>Conciliation Procedure": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "<1>Chapter X-A</1>Adjudix Lok Adalat": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "§ {0}A": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Nature of the Adjudix Lok Adalat": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The Adjudix Lok Adalat is a confidential settlement sitting of one day, which the parties may convene at any stage of a proceeding under this Code. It is inspired by the spirit of the Lok Adalat, but is not a Lok Adalat organised under the Legal Services Authorities Act, {0}.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The sitting is conducted as a conciliation, and the provisions of this Code on conciliation apply to it, subject to this Chapter.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "§ {0}B": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Appointment of the Lok Adalat Conciliator": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "On a joint request of the parties, the Secretariat shall appoint a conciliator from the Panel who has had no previous involvement in the dispute, and shall fix the date of the sitting.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "The conciliator shall make the disclosure required of a neutral under this Code and give a written undertaking of confidentiality before the sitting.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "§ {0}C": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Confidential Proposals and Settlement": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026",
 "Each party shall submit its proposal for settlement to the conciliator in a sealed or encrypted submission before the sitting. No proposal shall be disclosed to any other party, or to the neutral in the main proceeding.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2026"
}
